# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# node_modules is the load-bearing one: in a forest worktree web/node_modules is
# a SYMLINK to an absolute path in the main checkout, so `COPY web/ ./` either
# fails or lands a dangling link on top of the real modules `npm install` just
# created one step earlier. The image installs its own dependencies from
# package.json/package-lock.json, so the host tree's copy is never wanted.
node_modules
web/node_modules
**/node_modules

# Stale incremental-build state from the host would make `tsc -b` skip work it
# should redo inside the image.
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Python bytecode compiled against the host interpreter.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Never ship the live data volume into a build layer: it holds the application
# ledger, the canonical CV and the pre-deletion Jobs archive — personal data
# that has no business in an image. The volume is mounted at runtime instead.
data/

# Repository and tooling state the image has no use for.
.git
.gitignore
.aether/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
